{\rtf1\ansi{\fonttbl\f0 HelveticaNeue;\f1 Menlo-Regular;}\f0\tab\tab\tab\tab - \f1 None\f0  is a literal whose value is the lone representative of the \f1 NoneType\f0  class.\par\tab\tab\tab\tab - In programming, we need a way to express the absence of a value. In Python, we do this with \f1 None\f0 . It can also indicate missing, unset, or unavailable data and may sometimes be an error indication.\par}